## Start here

| I want to… | Do this |
|---|---|
| Work on the project | Open OpenCode here (the `project-manager` agent is the default) and use `/pm`, or a specialist command (`/ba`, `/dev`, …) |
| Know the current state | `/status` or read `docs/project/status/phase-state.md` |
| Start the lifecycle | `/pm` with your intent — Phase 1 begins with a Discovery gate pack |
| Ask about approved knowledge | `/ask <question>` (cited, read-only) |
| Feed new information | `/intake <source>` (staged, critic pass, you accept item-by-item) |
| Change the harness | Open a `harness-improvement` issue; after approval run `harness/scripts/apply-harness-change.ps1` |

## Layout

- `harness/` — core kit + scripts (never hand-edit to change rules; propose instead)
- `docs/harness/` — core harness specifications and decisions (project-agnostic)
- `project.yaml` — this project's configuration (the single per-project input)
- `docs/project/` — this project's workspace (knowledge, requirements, status, decisions)
- `.opencode/` — generated agents/commands · `.github/` — generated governance forms and workflows

## Safety

Agents cannot merge, push `main`, deploy, approve phases, or edit governance/config paths — those are owner actions enforced by permissions, policies, and GitHub. Secrets and sensitive data are permission-denied. See `docs/harness/security-and-permissions.md`.
